### 5. Summarise

As illustrated in @tbl-summarise, `dg_summary()` computes metrics for one table (size, columns, rows,
missing-value rate), and `dg_summarise()` does the same for many at once — even
an entire `dg_find_datasets()` result:


::: {#tbl-summarise .cell tbl-cap='Summary of the `iris` and `mtcars` datasets'}

```{.r .cell-code}
dg_summarise(datasets = list(iris = iris, mtcars = mtcars)) |> 
  gt::gt() |> 
  gt::cols_label(
    dataset = "Dataset",
    size_kb = "Size (KB)",
    n_vars = "Number of Variables",
    n_numeric = "Numeric Variables",
    n_non_numeric = "Non-numeric Variables",
    n_rows = "Number of Rows",
    prop_missing = "Missing Rate"
  ) |> 
  gt::fmt_number(columns = c("size_kb", "n_vars", "n_numeric", "n_non_numeric", "n_rows"), decimals = 0) |>
  gt::fmt_percent(columns = "prop_missing", decimals = 1) |>
  gt::opt_stylize(style = 4)
```

